<title>USA: Warming trend develops in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Warming trend develops in Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>High pressure that brought cool weather to Brazil's coffee belt the past few days is now heading out to sea, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Tuesday. A warming trend is expected to develop and continue thorugh the end of the week.</p>
<p>There were mostly fair skies observed this morning. Temperatures ranged below normal from 40-50 F (5-10 C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for today. Partly to variably cloudy skies are expected for Wednesday and Thrusday with the chance of a few light showers developing. Temperatures will turn milder, with lows mostly in the 50's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>The extended outlook calls for partly cloudy skies through Sunday and the chance of a few light showers next Monday. Temperatures should be near normal.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
